          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" b="1" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>STUDY OVERVIEW</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" b="1" dirty="0"/>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>This was a quasi-experimental pre-post study across 5 private not-for-profit faith-based hospitals in Kampala, Uganda: Nsambya, Lubaga, Mengo, Naguru, Kibuli.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Pre-intervention data (6,858 births) collected retrospectively from hospital records 2018-2022.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Post-intervention data (9,435 births) collected prospectively 2020-2025 as NRT was rolled out sequentially.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>ALL 16,293 deliveries were by caesarean section - findings apply specifically to CS deliveries.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>NRT BUNDLE: (1) standardised DR resuscitation protocols, (2) NRT member at every theatre delivery, (3) warm transport using exothermic mattresses, (4) structured NNU admission documentation, (5) equipment standardisation (CPAP circuits, nasal prongs, pulse oximeters, oxygen cylinders).</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
        </p:txBody>
